  1	# Diagram editor presentation — shared Light scope
  2	
  3	Contract version: 1.0.0. Guide version: 1.0. Owning change: `frade-light-diagram-editor`.
  4	
  5	This companion records the user-approved exception to Guide section 5.1 and
  6	Themes-and-Plugins Spec section 6. Their protected source files and canonical
  7	tokens are unchanged; the normative OpenSpec deltas define the scoped change.
  8	Current implementation/check coverage is reported in LIGHT-DIAGRAM-EDITOR-STATUS.md.
  9	This document does not imply completed integration, visual acceptance or POST.
 10	
 11	## Appearance and ownership
 12	
 13	The complete application-rendered Draw.io and native Frade diagram editor uses
 14	one shared Light presentation, including its own actions, panels, menus, dialogs,
 15	style controls and tooltips. Ordinary Light, Dark, System, High Contrast and
 16	VS Code Dark 2026 selection still controls the external workbench and global
 17	pickers. The reference geometry preset applies to the external workbench;
 18	comparable editor controls use the shared density/component contract.
 19	
 20	Windows forced colors has final priority. The editor reuses the existing
 21	resolver's validated system-color mapping and returns to Light on exit. Density
 22	is independent: compact/comfortable and coarse pointer targets use canonical
 23	shared tokens. No second resolver, registry, visual library or preference is added.
 24	
 25	The versioned role data is packages/ui-workspace/tokens/diagram-editor-presentation.json.
 26	It references the canonical Light palette and declares only the neutral canvas
 27	and decorative dot colors. Both engines keep their configured semantic grid size,
 28	visibility, phase, pan/zoom and snapping. The common scale-1 dot diameter is 1.2 CSS px.
 29	No routing algorithm, endpoint, persisted coordinate or author style changes are allowed.
 30	
 31	Each editor has an explicit root/ownership lease. A portaled editor-owned surface
 32	retains that lease inside the one managed overlay host; a global dialog is not
 33	made editor-owned merely because it overlaps the diagram. Disposal restores only
 34	owned projection fields, preserving subsequent owners. Unknown/disposed owners
 35	cannot restyle another editor or a global picker.
 36	
 37	## Atomic presentation and content
 38	
 39	Local Light is a derived participant-boundary view of the authoritative snapshot.
 40	The application identity, settings, revisions and transaction contexts remain in
 41	the existing controller. Parent chrome and canvas/frame share one registration
 42	and the service's painted neutral cover. They must both settle their actual paint
 43	ACK before publication. Prepare is side-effect-free. Abort, stale membership,
 44	rollback, parked-frame readiness and original deadlines remain mandatory.
 45	
 46	Authored fills, strokes, text, alpha, images, page styles and effective defaults
 47	remain content. UI rules must exclude SVG cell paint, palette swatches and style
 48	preview thumbnails. Never materialize author attributes or persist derived theme
 49	state to make appearance match. Compare matched supported attributes on the same
 50	backdrop; list unavailable native page/image/gradient capabilities explicitly.
 51	System file/color pickers and native prompts remain OS-owned surfaces.
 52	
 53	## Evidence and rollout
 54	
 55	The incremental rollout is shared profile/composition, native retained root,
 56	frame/bridge, owned surfaces, then full current interaction/visual coverage.
 57	Partial unit GREEN is not application integration or visual approval. Required
 58	runtime, performance, accessibility, unchanged-document/undo, source replay and
 59	independent POST checks remain in the owning verification.md. Preserve historic
 60	FAILs and existing origin pins. New baselines need explicit visual acceptance.
